Allow the HTTP/2 flow-control test more time on slower SPARC systems.

The test validates connection reuse after closing a buffered response, not the
session timeout itself.  Its two-second limit expires before the follow-up
response arrives on SPARC, while adjacent flow-control tests take substantially
longer there.

Not suitable for upstream.

--- a/tests/http2-test.c
+++ b/tests/http2-test.c
@@ -731,7 +731,11 @@ do_flow_control_close_buffered_body_test (Test *test, gconstpointer data)
         GError *error = NULL;
         WindowSize window_size = { -1, REALLY_LARGE_BUFFER_SIZE };
 
+#ifdef __sparc
+        soup_session_set_timeout (test->session, 30);
+#else
         soup_session_set_timeout (test->session, 2);
+#endif
 
         closed_uri = g_uri_parse_relative (base_uri, "/larger-than-window", SOUP_HTTP_URI_FLAGS, NULL);
         closed_msg = soup_message_new_from_uri (SOUP_METHOD_GET, closed_uri);
